  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=2{e}^{1-\\theta }$ for $0\\le \\theta \\le \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2{e}^{1-\\theta }$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}(2{e}^{1-\\theta })^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}4{e}^{2-2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}{e}^{-2\\theta }\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}(-\\frac{{e}^{-2\\theta }}{2}){|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{2}({e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-{e}^{2}(\\frac{1}{9}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
